---
// Lesson 8.6 — Boss Studio + Final Review
// Studio polish + semester-1 review; the final is "just a normal B day."
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>8.6 — Boss Studio + Final Review</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Your boss works (<a href="8.5.html">8.5</a>), and the semester's
    final is "just a normal B day" — a normal B day where you ship
    the fight you have been building toward since September. Today:
    final polish in the morning, and the review that makes you ready
    to talk about everything you own.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Studio Brief</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Polish, from the spec.</strong> Open your
    <a href="8.1.html">8.1</a> BOSS_SPEC.md and grade yourself
    line by line. Every attack has a telegraph? Phase changes are
    visible within one second? The arena has exactly the hazards you
    promised? Then the three universal upgrades:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sound:</strong> a hit sound on player swing
            connect, a wind-up sound on charge, a death sound.
            Audio is half of "feel" and zero of "mechanics"</li>
        <li><strong>Hit feedback:</strong> boss flash
            (<a href="8.3.html">8.3</a> tinker), camera shake on
            charge</li>
        <li><strong>The clear screen:</strong> when the boss dies,
            a UI text "CAVE CLEAR" (a trigger + your HUD family) —
            games end with a statement, not silence</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Ship freeze rules for the review:</strong> no new
    attacks, no new systems, no "just one more mechanic." New
    things break old things; the final build must be your most
    boring build.</p>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Bug Hunt: The final sweep</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Full playthrough, spawn to boss door: entrance →
                all six cave beats (<a href="7.5.html">7.5</a>)
                → the fight → the clear screen. Write every bug
                on paper as you go; fix them ONLY after the run.</li>
            <li>Coin economy check: how many coins can a full
                run collect, and what did
                <a href="2.1.html">2.1</a>'s death loop pay on a
                wipe? Does death still feel cheap enough to keep
                trying?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity assessment">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Final Review</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        The final is a normal B day: your game, open, playable, and
        a conversation about it. Practice that conversation — answer
        each in 30 seconds OUT LOUD:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>Trace a click on a coin to the counter on screen — name
            every method it passes through
            (<a href="2.1.html">2.1</a>)</li>
        <li>Draw your boss's state machine from memory
            (<a href="4.5.html">4.5</a> + <a href="8.2.html">8.2</a>)</li>
        <li>Explain deltaTime to someone who has never coded
            (<a href="1.5.html">1.5</a>)</li>
        <li>Why is your jump "tight"? Say the three tunables
            (<a href="6.3.html">6.3</a>)</li>
        <li>Where did YOU use the cooldown pattern — count every
            instance in your game (turret, enemy damage, your
            swing, and…?)</li>
        <li>What does the UnityEvent on your boss's death decouple
            (<a href="5.2.html">5.2</a>, <a href="8.5.html">8.5</a>)</li>
        <li>Which beat of your cave killed the most playtesters —
            and what is the data (<a href="7.7.html">7.7</a>)</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic</h3>
        <p>
            One more for the road: your whole game is a program
            built by forking a starter. What did you INHERIT
            (unchanged), what did you EXTEND (changed via knobs),
            and what did you CREATE (new code)? Where is the line
            between "using a library" and "authorship"? That
            question is Unit 10's jam and Unit 11's Create PT
            rolled together.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: Ship it</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Build (File → Build Settings → your platform) or
                just pin the scene open on the lab machine — the
                final is the playable game, not the code</li>
            <li>Tag the release: <code>git tag semester-1 &amp;&amp; git push --tags</code></li>
            <li>Commit + push: <code>"8.6a: semester-1 shipped"</code></li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — the semester, complete:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Spawn-to-boss full run is bug-free enough to demo to a stranger</li>
            <li>Spec graded line by line; every gap has a reason, not an excuse</li>
            <li>All seven review answers said out loud without notes</li>
            <li>Repo tagged and pushed — the playable is the portfolio</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-08/index.html">Unit 8: Boss Fight</a> — the ship checklist</li>
        <li><a href="../index.html">Dashboard</a> — the whole semester at a glance</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next unit: <a href="9.1.html">9.1 — Binary: How Numbers Live in Memory</a> — how it all works underneath.</p>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="8.6" title="8.6a Boss Studio + Final Review — AP CS Principles" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
